00:34:48.000 --> 00:35:33.000
arrest, and he instructed his detectives to do so, certain they would be able to break him. But after the arrest, an attorney called the station and asked to speak to the mechanic. She was organised by his girlfriend, and she instructed him to stop talking to the police immediately. And he did. From that point on, he never said another word. Because he stopped talking, Souza and the detectives were forced to go to the prosecutor with what they had, hoping they would be given approval to charge the mechanic with murder. But they weren't. The prosecutor advised there was insufficient evidence. If it went to trial, they feared there was a good chance the mechanic would be acquitted, meaning they could never

